  "notes": "A club kick on all four quarters with a rapper on top — the electro half of the four-on-floor/trap-grid alternation research names, with the trap grid it cuts back to kept as a mood of its own. What separates it from house is the harmony: harmonic minor stated outright, the raised seventh leaning into a major V, arpeggiated in 16ths by a trance pluck while a gated supersaw carries the hook. The 808 is an accent, not the bassline — a real synth bass pushes the offbeat eighths in the holes between the kicks, and the FX layer (riser, impact, reverse, crash) is structural rather than garnish — a riser and an impact are how this music hands one section to the next.",
